{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"release lock-in follow-up","verdict":"block","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"R-003","severity":"medium","summary":"The repair and updated fallback description are accurate for non-default branches, but the unqualified uniqueness claim overstates the guarantee.","evidence":["The router returns no token for `main`, `master`, `trunk`, and `develop`; those branches use the shared `followup` naming sequence instead.","The notes say “Distinct branches share a record name only on a hash-prefix collision,” then state that on a default branch or detached HEAD the counter remains. Separate worktrees on distinct default branches can select the same counter-based record name."],"action":"Qualify the uniqueness claim as applying to non-default branches, and say that the default-branch and detached-HEAD counter can still produce shared names across worktrees."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"The prior slugless-branch omission in R-003.","bin":"repaired for non-default branches","disposition":"The notes now say that a name whose slug is empty becomes `branch`; the router and test confirm that fallback. The raw-branch hash and prefix-collision caveat are also described."},{"concern":"Regression to prior dispositions R-001, R-002, R-004, R-005, or R-006.","bin":"no regression identified","disposition":"The packet says the other five selected inputs are unchanged; this review did not reassess those prior dispositions."}],"next_move":"Narrow the uniqueness claim to non-default branches and retain the stated counter behavior for default branches and detached HEADs.","non_claims":["Reviewed the six identity-bound inline semantic inputs; did not inspect workspace paths or run tests.","The hashed naming guarantee is subject to 8-hex hash-prefix collisions."]}
